# ---------------- Upgrades.events (Task 27 Part D) ----------------
# The RTS upgrade table: how long a research takes, what it costs, which building may run it
# and how many levels it has. It is read by name — Upgrades.events — once at load and again on
# hot reload, the same way Matchups.events and Resources.events are.
#
# HOW A LINE IS READ: `<Upgrade>Time` (seconds), `<Upgrade>Cost` (the default cost resource,
# Minerals unless Resources.events says otherwise), `<Upgrade>Requires` (the building template
# that may research it) and `<Upgrade>Levels` (how high it goes; 1 when nobody says). The name is
# whatever comes before the suffix, so `StimPackTime` defines the upgrade `Stim Pack` /
# `StimPack` — `research "Stim Pack" at Barracks` matches it.
#
# WHAT FINISHING DOES: `Player<N> <Upgrade>` goes up by one through the tech table, so the
# upgrade lands for the building's owner only. Units read it on spawn (`when me appears`) or when
# it changes (`when Player1 StimPack changes`), e.g.
#   when Player1 StimPack changes
#     set my Speed to 120
#
# CHANGING IT AT RUNTIME: these are ordinary globals first — any sheet may `set StimPackTime to
# 45`, and the live global wins over the row below. A scene that never researches is unaffected.

when game starts
  # ---- Stim Pack: a cheap early upgrade (Marine.events spends it) -------------------------
  set StimPackTime to 30
  set StimPackCost to 100
  set StimPackRequires to "Barracks"
  set StimPackLevels to 1

  # ---- Psi Storm: the templar ability's prerequisite research ------------------------------
  set PsiStormTime to 45
  set PsiStormCost to 200
  set PsiStormRequires to "TemplarArchives"
  set PsiStormLevels to 1

  # ---- Weapon and armour upgrades: repeatable, three levels each -------------------------
  set InfantryWeaponsTime to 40
  set InfantryWeaponsCost to 100
  set InfantryWeaponsRequires to "Barracks"
  set InfantryWeaponsLevels to 3

  set InfantryArmorTime to 40
  set InfantryArmorCost to 100
  set InfantryArmorRequires to "Barracks"
  set InfantryArmorLevels to 3
